messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S04
Scenario title: Defect Issue Triage and Risk Reporting
Initial workflow description:
When a defect occurs, the engineer reports it, discusses it with related teams, performs additional experiments, and decides how to improve the issue and communicate the risk.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What specific event or signal triggers the defect reporting step — for example, is it an automated system alert, a failed test result, a manual observation by an engineer, or something else?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "Which teams or roles are typically involved in the discussion step after a defect is reported, and who holds the final authority to approve the chosen improvement action?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "What do the 'additional experiments' involve — what types of tests or analyses are performed, and what outcome or condition signals that this step is complete?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "Is there a defined framework, scoring model, or risk matrix used to evaluate the defect and decide on the improvement approach, or is this judgment left to individual engineers?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "What does the risk communication output look like — who receives it, in what format is it delivered, and are there required fields or a standard template that must be followed?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "Is there a separate escalation or fast-track path for high-severity defects, and if so, how is severity determined and what steps differ from the standard workflow?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Triage a defect issue, coordinate investigation, and report improvement actions and customer risk.",
  "actors": [
    "issue owner",
    "process engineer",
    "quality engineer",
    "customer interface owner",
    "manager"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "issue tracking system",
    "experiment log",
    "risk report template",
    "collaboration tool"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "defect description",
    "sample or lot context",
    "initial evidence",
    "customer impact assumption"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "issue report",
    "root-cause hypothesis",
    "experiment plan",
    "improvement action",
    "customer risk summary"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Register defect issue with initial evidence",
      "actor": "issue owner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Classify issue severity and affected scope",
      "actor": "quality engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Notify related teams and assign owners",
      "actor": "issue owner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Define root-cause hypotheses",
      "actor": "process engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Plan and run follow-up experiment",
      "actor": "process engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Review experiment result and select improvement action",
      "actor": "issue owner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Assess customer risk",
      "actor": "customer interface owner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A8",
      "name": "Share final report and action items",
      "actor": "manager"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Is the issue customer-impacting?",
      "branches": [
        "customer risk exists",
        "internal issue only"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Does the experiment support the root-cause hypothesis?",
      "branches": [
        "supported",
        "not supported"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "insufficient evidence",
    "unclear owner",
    "experiment delay",
    "conflicting root-cause hypotheses"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A7",
      "to": "A8",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A1",
      "rationale": "Issue reports can be pre-structured from defect descriptions and evidence attachments."
    },
    {
      "target": "A3",
      "rationale": "Related teams can be suggested from issue category and affected process area."
    },
    {
      "target": "A8",
      "rationale": "Action-item extraction and risk report drafting can be partially automated."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}
